# Order #{{.ID.Num}}

**{{ orderSays .Order }}** · placed {{ .PlacedTS.Format "2 Jan 2006, 15:04" }}

{{if .Paid -}}
--panel[padding=16, margin=0 0 16 0, border=2, color=accent, radius=8]--
## Payment complete

Your {{ money .Total }}{{ with .TotalDCR }} ({{ . }}){{ end }} has arrived and
this order is paid for. Nothing more is needed from you.

The seller is preparing it now, and you are told here when it goes out. If
you need to say anything about it, the messages at the bottom of this page
reach them.

{{template "txref.tmpl" .}}
--/panel--

{{- /*
What happens next, and the refund address.

The address used to be asked for on the way in -- first under the payment
cards, then on the review page -- and in both places it read as "this might
go wrong" at the moment the buyer was deciding whether to trust the shop at
all. Here it is what it actually is: a detail for the unlikely case, given by
somebody who has already paid and is no longer deciding anything.
*/}}

## What happens next

--panel[padding=14, margin=0 0 8 0, border=1, color=outline, radius=8]--
**When does it arrive?**

{{ if .ShipAddr }}The seller posts it to the address below. They mark the
order as sent when it goes, and you see that on this page.
{{- else }}The seller sends it to you here in Bison Relay. Anything they owe
you as a file arrives on its own; anything else they arrange with you in the
messages at the bottom of this page.
{{- end }}
--/panel--

--panel[padding=14, margin=0 0 8 0, border=1, color=outline, radius=8]--
**What if something is wrong with it?**

Say so in the messages at the bottom of this page. They go to the seller and
they stay attached to this order, so neither of you has to remember which one
it was about.
--/panel--

{{if .OnChain}}
--panel[padding=14, margin=0 0 8 0, border=1, color=outline, radius=8]--
**What if it has to be sent back?**

If money ever has to come back to you, an address here is where it goes. It
is optional, and the seller can ask you for one in the messages instead.

--form--
type="action" value="/setRefund/{{.ID}}"
type="txtinput" label="Refund address" name="refund_addr" value="{{.RefundAddr}}"
type="submit" label="{{ if .RefundAddr }}Change it{{ else }}Save it{{ end }}"
--/form--
--/panel--
{{end}}
{{ else if .PaymentSeen -}}
--panel[padding=16, margin=0 0 16 0, border=1, color=accent, radius=8]--
## Your payment has been seen

It is waiting for a confirmation from the network, which usually takes a few
minutes. Nothing more is needed from you, and you do not have to stay on this
page — the shop is watching for it and will mark the order when it arrives.

{{template "txref.tmpl" .}}
--/panel--
{{ else if and .PayURI .OnChain -}}
## Pay {{ money .Total }}{{ with .TotalDCR }} — {{ . }}{{ end }}

{{template "paypanel.tmpl" .}}

{{- /*
The clock, counted where there is one.

The page said "another 21 minutes" and went on saying it: a page is fetched
once and nothing tells it the time. At nought it stops being a warning and
becomes what happened, with one press to start again at today's rate. See
markdown_countdown.dart.
*/}}
{{ with .ExpiresInSeconds }}
--countdown[seconds={{.}}, link=/reorder/{{ $.ID }}, label=Order it again]--
{{ end }}

{{ else if .PayURI -}}
## Pay {{ money .Total }}{{ with .TotalDCR }} — {{ . }}{{ end }}

--panel[full=on, padding=16, margin=0 0 8 0, border=1, color=accent, radius=8, text=center, help=Paid from the Bison Relay wallet in this app. Lightning settles the moment it goes through, so the seller sees it immediately and there is nothing to wait for.]--
**Pay with your Bison Relay wallet**

{{ .PayURI }}
--/panel--

{{- /*
The clock, counted where there is one.

The page said "another 21 minutes" and went on saying it: a page is fetched
once and nothing tells it the time. At nought it stops being a warning and
becomes what happened, with one press to start again at today's rate. See
markdown_countdown.dart.
*/}}
{{ with .ExpiresInSeconds }}
--countdown[seconds={{.}}, link=/reorder/{{ $.ID }}, label=Order it again]--
{{ end }}
{{ else if .Expired -}}
--panel[padding=16, margin=0 0 16 0, border=1, color=outline, radius=8]--
The amount this order was quoted at no longer holds. Ask the seller below
and they can place it again at today's rate.
--/panel--
{{ end -}}

{{- /*
The files this order bought, with a way into each of them.

The shop sends them the moment payment lands and they arrive in Files >
Purchases like anything else. Which left the buyer on a page that said a file
was on its way and then said nothing else -- no way to know whether it came,
and a section of the app to go and look in. Where a file landed is a fact
about the buyer's own machine, so the page names what was bought and their
client answers. See markdown_purchase.dart.
*/}}
{{ if .Fulfilled }}{{ with .Goods }}
